      <Docs>
        <summary>
            Gets or sets the placeholder name shown in usage help for the argument's value.
            The value will be wrapped in angle brackets (<c>&lt;</c> and <c>&gt;</c>).
            </summary>
        <value>
            The name to show as the placeholder for the argument's value.
            </value>
        <remarks>
            If <c>null</c>, the <see cref="P:System.CommandLine.Symbol.Name" /> of the argument will be used.
            </remarks>
        <example>
            An argument with <see cref="P:System.CommandLine.Symbol.Name" /> of <c>argument</c> and a
            <see cref="P:System.CommandLine.Argument.HelpName" /> of <c>Value</c> will be shown in usage help as:
            <c>&lt;Value&gt;</c>. If <see cref="P:System.CommandLine.Argument.HelpName" /> is not set,
            help output will show: <c>&lt;argument&gt;</c>.
            </example>
      </Docs>
